            Training Tip
          </p>
          <p class="text-amber-800 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Hold the handrails only when you truly need them, like during the
            first few sessions at a new steep grade. Gripping the rails
            reduces the number of calories you burn and takes your core and
            glutes out of the equation, which defeats much of the point of
            incline training in the first place. Use them briefly for
            balance, then let go once you find your rhythm.
          </p>
